' ── HOW THIS ORDER WAS REACHED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' 2026-11-10. Eight read-only lanes mapped the seams (61 slices before
' de-duplication, 61 corrections to the two plans, since applied). Two of them
' settled the Bubble Tea v2 unknowns, one by reading the library and one by
' running it under tmux. Three planners then ordered the 50 de-duplicated
' slices under different lenses, and three judges scored each ordering.
' Five slices changed afterwards. The prompt kit added S9, S10 and S11. D9
' retired B1 (the cell grid) and added B11 (golden frames). D8 added B12 (the
' Go bump). That makes 54 ids: 52 in waves and 2 deferred.
'   lens         dependencies   operator value   verification
'   fix-first        22              21               19      chosen by all three
'   risk-first       21              17               19
'   write-once       14              15               15
' (five criteria, 1 to 5 each.) No ordering broke a dependency edge.
' write-once puts the fix for the reported freeze 21st of 50 to save about 20
' lines; its own author flags that as too late.
' This file is fix-first with the judges' grafts: the gates and the tagged
' oracles first (write-once, risk-first), a Linux leg written as commands,
' deletions one wave behind their proof (risk-first), the button confirms
' directly behind the modal port (write-once).
' Every measurement behind it ran on darwin/arm64, go1.26.5, tmux 3.7b.
' [Unverified] Nothing has run on Linux. W1 is the first wave that does.
'
