' ── THE STANDING GATE — EVERY WAVE, BEFORE ITS PR MERGES ───────────────────
' Green means NO NEW FAILING TEST (D12, the Executor). `mise run ci` exits
' non-zero on this host at main, so its three parts run as separate lines:
'   1  mise run lint
'   2  go build ./...
'   3  mise run baseline        # one `go test -race -count=1 -json ./...`;
'      exits 1 on a failing test outside cmd/proveo-dev/unit-baseline.txt, or
'      on a package that fails with no failing test of its own (G0, landed
'      2026-11-10 as a proveo-dev command instead of a jq line:
'      _spec/_devops/unit-baseline.puml)
'   4  go vet -tags=e2e ./e2e/                           # until G2 lands
'   5  GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...          # until G3 lands
'   6  plantuml -checkonly <every .puml the wave edits>
'   7  each tagged run uses -v, and its output holds no line matching
'      `^--- SKIP` and no "no tests to run": a skip or an empty match is not a
'      pass (release-gate.puml records that misread)
'   8  mise run build-cli && proveo --version            # dev@<HEAD>, then
'      the wave's hand trial in a host terminal tab
' THE BASELINE, MEASURED at 0f34a714 (= main) with and without -race: 15 tests
' in 3 of 47 packages; the names are in _spec/_devops/unit-baseline.puml. Two fail
' on any host. TestVarsSortByScopeThenName guards envreg.go, which S1 may edit:
' fix envreg.go:153 in the first slice that touches that file.
' ONE PR PER WAVE. History here is squash-merged, so a wave reverts as one
' commit. Lanes inside a wave are commits on the wave's branch.
' e2e runs name their tests with -run. Three live sandboxes share this host; a
' bare e2e run starts real sandboxes beside them.
' THE LINUX LEG. From W1 on, each wave reruns its -race unit suites and its
' tmux pins inside a Linux proveo sandbox (docker and tmux, no sbx).
' [Unverified] That sandbox has python3: defs/base/Dockerfile names tmux only,
' and TestLiveCtrlCConfirmationOnTmux skips without it. B3 rewrites that
' test's helper anyway and replaces the python child with the re-executed test
' binary, so the pin needs tmux alone.
' THE WAY BACK for an operator whose terminal misdraws a ported surface: the
' existing PROVEO_WIZARD=off path, which every page keeps (the headless rule).
