note bottom of W0
  **Oracles before changes.** No lane ran a
  tagged e2e test. W0 runs the tmux pins once,
  unchanged, so a pin already red is not
  charged to the wave that follows.
end note

note bottom of W1
  **The fix needs no library.** It lands ninth:
  seven gate and teardown slices and its own
  first half come before it. It waits on
  nothing in the port.
end note

note bottom of W2
  **The slice that can lose work silently.** A
  dropped step shows only in real-sbx clone
  suites. T2's logged step order, captured in
  W0, is diffed after the refactor.
end note

note bottom of W3
  **Every measured defect is fixed here.** Four
  waves, thirteen slices, the current stack.
  A failed port after this point costs no
  fix that already shipped.
end note

note bottom of W4
  **Alone, and invisible.** The gate passed on
  macOS under tmux only. If it fails on Linux
  or in another terminal, one PR reverts and
  the tcell overlay is still there.
end note

note bottom of W8
  **Verbs first, then the prompt.** A segment
  that reads "2 to adopt" with no command to
  lower it is a half-shipped surface, so the
  kit follows the verbs by a wave.
end note

note bottom of W10
  **Three call sites, three files.** The tree
  replaces one picker. tcell leaves go.mod
  only after the attach list, proveo-dev's
  multi-select and the windows stub move.
end note

note bottom of LINUX
  **Every number so far is macOS.** The cancel
  path, the process-group kill and the gate
  have no Linux run. Each wave from W1 reruns
  its pins in a Linux sandbox.
end note

